| [docker-compose.yml](file:///c:/Users/DELL%20E5570%20i5/Desktop/dynamic-pricing-engine/docker-compose.yml) | API (8000) + Dashboard (8501) |
| [README.md](file:///c:/Users/DELL%20E5570%20i5/Desktop/dynamic-pricing-engine/README.md) | Professional README with badges, architecture, API docs |

## How to Run

```bash
# API
uvicorn src.api:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000

# Dashboard (new terminal)
streamlit run dashboard/app.py --server.port 8501

# Or with Docker
docker-compose up --build
```

> [!NOTE]
> Both API and dashboard use XGBoost's native `feature_importances_` (weighted by input values) for real-time top factors instead of SHAP, which was too slow for request-time computation. The full SHAP analysis remains available in the pre-generated plots at `outputs/model/`.
